      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the young woman shown in <Picture 1> and <Picture 2>: an Asian girl with dark hair worn up, a red-and-white flower ornament pinned at the left side of her head, large bright eyes and fair skin. She wears a navy-blue yukata printed with fireworks and floral patterns, a wide red obi sash tied at her waist, and geta sandals with red straps. Her hair, ornament, yukata, obi and sandals stay exactly as shown in the reference images in every frame.\n<Audio 1> is the singing voice of <Subject 1> (S1): a music recording that already contains her vocal track together with its instrumental backing. Use <Audio 1> exactly as it is, keeping its original melody, pitch and tempo.\n<Subject 2> is the environment: a Japanese summer festival ground at night. Golden and pink fireworks keep blooming in the deep blue sky. Rows of red and warm-yellow paper lanterns hang overhead, festival stalls glow along both sides, and a blurred crowd moves in the distance. She stands on a stone-paved plaza. The look is warm lantern light against a cool night sky.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation + audio reference] <Subject 1> dances and performs to a Japanese summer\nfestival song in <Subject 2>, a festival ground at night, in a single continuous shot driven by\n<Audio 1>.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - her hairstyle, flower ornament, navy yukata,\nred obi and geta sandals are retained throughout.\n<Audio 1>: copied exactly - the entire clip is used unchanged, including its melody, pitch and instrumental backing.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - the same outdoor festival ground is kept, and\nthe relative positions of the lanterns, stalls and plaza stay consistent.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is a realistic, cinematic music-video shot, lit by warm lantern light against a\ncool night sky. A golden firework blooms in the night sky behind her as the chorus opens.\n[Shot 1] She throws both arms open and spins a full turn in place, the long navy sleeves flaring out with the rotation, singing as she turns, <d>[Chinese] 花火开 我就转圈圈</d>. Her sleeve sweeps close past the lens as she comes back around to face the camera, and she sings, <d>[Chinese] 蓝色的袖 飞过你眼前</d>. She beckons to the camera and claps on the beat, calling the viewer to follow her, singing, <d>[Chinese] 咚咚咚 咚咚咚 跟上我</d>. Her lips open clearly on every syllable she sings, her jaw and cheeks moving naturally with the pronunciation, teeth briefly visible on some words, and her mouth staying open through sustained notes.\nThe camera tracks around her in an arc, letting the flying sleeve pass in front of the lens during her spin, then returns to a frontal medium shot. The camera stays close enough that her facial expression remains clearly readable.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nA summer festival ground at night, with a distant crowd and stall ambience.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\n<Audio 1> already contains the backing music - festival taiko drums, shamisen and an electronic\nbeat - and its original instrumentation and mix are kept.\n",
        736,
        1312,
        243,
        "match"
      ]
